I"�<h2 id="about-this-course">About This Course</h2>

<p>A Cloud Center of Excellence (CCoE) is the organizational construct that enables enterprises to adopt, manage, and optimize cloud at scale. This course explores how to build one, what it should own, and how to make it an accelerator rather than a bottleneck.</p>

<h2 id="what-youll-learn">What You’ll Learn</h2>

<ul>
  <li>What a Cloud Center of Excellence is and why enterprises need one</li>
  <li>How to structure and staff a CCoE for your organization’s size and maturity</li>
  <li>The relationship between a CCoE and individual product teams</li>
  <li>Cloud governance frameworks the CCoE should own</li>
  <li>How to measure the CCoE’s impact and demonstrate its value</li>
  <li>Common CCoE failure modes and how to avoid them</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="who-this-is-for">Who This Is For</h2>

<p>Enterprise IT leaders, cloud architects, and technology executives responsible for cloud strategy, governance, and adoption at scale.</p>
